{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Because of violence</b> — these verses indicate that this prophecy concerning Edom is after the exile of Jerusalem to Babylonia. So too the lamenter said: 'Remember, O YHWH, against the children of Edom, who said to the Babylonians, Strip her' [Lamentations]. And it is written: 'Your iniquity is completed, O daughter of Zion; He will no more exile you' [Lamentations 4:22], [then immediately] 'Your iniquity is punished, O daughter of Edom' [Lamentations 4:22]. And Nebuchadnezzar destroyed Edom, and its land became a desolation. And so Ezekiel prophesied, for Jerusalem returned after the Babylonian exile but Edom did not return. And it has already been explained in the book of Daniel, for Israel is not in the exile of Edom. And the interpretation of the ancients: the kingdom of Greece." "Now the sense of <b>because of violence</b> — because of the violence that Greece did to Israel on the day of Jerusalem."], :book :obadiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The cryptic reference 'the book of Daniel' as proving Israel is not in 'the exile of Edom' is left as Ibn Ezra gives it; his point is compressed and no connective tissue has been supplied."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Obadiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=18&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:34.835814717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}